### Was there a federal law or uniform rule in the 2020 US election that mandated all mail-in ballots postmarked by Election Day be accepted if received within a certain number of days after?
Answer: No, there was no federal law or uniform rule in the 2020 US election that mandated all mail-in ballots postmarked by Election Day be accepted if received within a certain number of days after; instead, deadlines varied by state, with some states using a "postmarked by" deadline (e.g., California accepting ballots postmarked by Election Day and received within 17 days) and others using a "received-by" deadline (e.g., Michigan requiring ballots to be received by 8:00 p.m. on Election Day).

